24 < 1 - Modify: `ledger/core.py`
25 < 1 
26 < 1 **Claim:** An operator asks which entry moved the most money, in either direction, and reads its memo. (derived)
27 < 1 Machine: M1. `biggest_memo("2026-09-01,rent,-5000,landlord\n2026-09-02,card,900,pay\n")` is exactly `"landlord"`.
28 < 1 
29 < 1 **Authorized-by:** operator's pick, 2026-11-13
30 < 1 
31 < 1 **Interfaces:**
32 < 1 - Consumes: nothing
33 < 1 - Produces: `biggest_memo(text: str) -> str`
34 < 1 
35 < 1 **Context:** `load(text)` answers a list of dicts with the keys `date`, `account`, `amt` and `memo`, and the module's `largest(entries)` already answers the dict whose `amt` is furthest from zero, so `biggest_memo` is `largest(load(text))["memo"]`.
36 < 1 
